import Battle.Types

/-!
# Learnsets — every species' legal move pool, transcribed 1:1

The set of moves each species can legally know, from pokered. For internal
species index `i`, `learnset i` unions:

* the level-1 starting moves (`data/pokemon/base_stats/*.asm`, `; level 1 learnset`),
* the level-up moves (`data/pokemon/evos_moves.asm`, the `db level, move` list),
* the TM/HM moves it is compatible with (the `tmhm` list in its base_stats file),
* and — transitively — the pools of all its **pre-evolutions**, because Gen-1
  Pokémon keep their moves through evolution (`GetMonHeader`/`LearnMove` never
  strip a move on evolve). So e.g. Gyarados inherits Magikarp's Splash/Tackle.

This is the level-agnostic "can this species ever legally hold this move" oracle
that `Battle/RL/LegalTeam.Dex.canLearn` consumes — the union crosses only
real-species evolution edges, so MissingNo/glitch pools never leak in. Keyed by
the internal index the party structs store (the model's `SpeciesId`).

Emitted by a deterministic parser over pret/pokered @
`405b6246372d7e5a2cb029cbb65219b13286b8c9`. `Battle.Rom.Tables` independently
decodes `EvosMovesPointerTable`, level-one moves, level-up payloads, TM/HM
bitfields, and evolution edges; `RequiredTableBytes.learnPools` certifies the
re-derived 191-entry array against this one.
-/

namespace Battle.Data

